 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "PLACE_ON_PATTERN and BUILD_PATTERN speak the pattern material by its registry name when it is not the concept's own item: a PILLAR of dark_oak_planks reads '짙은 참나무 판자 기둥 위에 …' even though the step teaches 판자 (a second taught word does not change this). nachtwache s2 therefore carries an authored clue ('밤에 달이 떠요. 판자 기둥 위에 하얀색 초를 놓아요.'). w1_08 s2 keeps the generated '짙은 참나무 판자 울타리 옆에 문을 달아요' (one compound unknown word) because the authored version could not say 달아요.",
  "QuestlineValidationTest.authoredCluesNameTheAction accepts only 놓/심/걸/깔 for PlaceOnPattern and PlaceRel, while PlaceBlock also accepts 달: the natural authored clue '판자 벽 옆에 문을 달아요' for a door beside a wall is rejected. A RING of planks is still spoken as 울타리 (the house walls read 벽 in s1 of w1_08 and 울타리 in s2).",
  "USE_BLOCK on a candle has no 'light' verb: the verb table gives 쓰다 and the action check for authored UseBlock clues wants 사용/자/열/울/먹/마시/대/누르/당기/써. '초를 켜요' is rejected, so w1_01 says '밤에 초에 불을 대요.' (finale line authored as well). A SWITCH_ON (켜다) rule for candles, campfires and lamps would fix it.",
  "A taught flower word covers every flower id: with teach sunflower, PLACE_REL dandelion NEXT_TO sunflower is spoken '해바라기 옆에 해바라기를 심어요' (the object takes the taught word). w1_03 s3 is authored ('해바라기 옆에 민들레를 심어요.').",
  "PLAYER_REL with a tag anchor (#minecraft:wool_carpets) is spoken '그것 위에서' (wave 3 item 13 is still open). w1_07 s3 uses the block anchor oak_log ('통나무 옆에서 달콤한 열매를 먹어요').",
  "TIME DUSK lasts 1000 ticks (50 s) and DAWN 2000 ticks, so they are unusable on early steps of a trail. The batch uses DAY and NIGHT; the only DAWN step is the finale of w1_08 (sleeping in the new bed ends the night at dawn).",
  "SMELT of a non-food output is spoken '화로에서 돌을 만들어요' (no input shown, no 구워/녹여 below the chain level); the first-furnace finale of adv_story_mine_stone cannot say that cobblestone is smelted into stone.",
  "A covered colour variant of a non-first object is spoken by its registry name, so the taught word is not recycled: '하늘색 양탄자를 깔아요' (light_blue_carpet) does not count as an encounter of 양탄자, and the generated hint needs an authored line (WaveQaTest, w1_07 s1).",
  "Signatures ignore the count, so a plain step on an object that another trail already asks for is a duplicate (CRAFT bread, CRAFT candle, CRAFT torch, CRAFT campfire, CRAFT glass_pane, SMELT glass, DIG sand, COLLECT dandelion). The batch separates them with a TIME, IN_BIOME or HOLDING condition, which also makes the sentence longer; a real 'how many' or 'where from' field would be a better handle.",
  "The relation-giveaway check for German uses \\b, which is ASCII only in Java: 'tagsüber' contains the word 'über' and is rejected in a relation step ('Breite am Tag einen Teppich aus' is used instead).",
  "No goal speaks a trade: there is no 사다/팔다 yet (generator wave 3 is still open), so the market of marktpfad is give bread (이야기해요. 빵을 줘요.) and collect emeralds. The cow comes first for the milk (GIVE wheat, then DRINK milk_bucket with PLAYER_REL cow); the bucket and the cow are the only parts that need iron.",
  "A clock (nachtwache s3, HOLDING) needs gold and redstone and a candle needs honeycomb (shears), so these two trails lean on items that are not strictly day-one; the brief asked for both."
 ]
